RED on 6f3dc7c (10 failures, evidence/A5a_red.txt): the three
endpoint-id construction sites (builder.ensure_endpoint, builder
observation-link, models.apply_observation) built the identity from
f"{host}{path}" — scheme and port were DROPPED. https/http on the
same host+path collapsed into ONE entity (evidence merged across
different trust boundaries); implicit vs explicit ports collapsed the
same way; methods_seen was REPLACED by the losing record's value on
the provenance tie-break; metadata carried only host/path.

Fix — the SSOT pair in builder.py:
* _endpoint_tuple_key(url) -> (scheme, host, effective_port, path) |
  None — effective_port is the explicit port or the scheme default
  (http->80, https->443) so https://h/x == https://h:443/x and
  http://h/x != https://h/x; a URL without scheme+host (bare
  host/path included) has NO identity -> the caller ABSTAINS.
* _endpoint_id_of(url) — the id minted from the tuple, used by BOTH
  build paths and apply_observation.
* add_entity merge path: methods_seen ACCUMULATES (set semantics,
  independent of the provenance winner); status_code keeps the LATEST
  (current state); identity facets carried explicitly.

GREEN: 12/12 (evidence/A5a_green.txt). Expected follow-up: the four
43C incremental tests pin legacy host+path ids (handled in the gates
commit per the batch prompt §6).
